Given below is the sketch of a program that represents the path in a two-person game tree (Minimax algorithm). The program uses mode = MAX for player-1's move and mode = MIN for player-2's move.

function search(B: boardtype; mode: modetype): real;
var C: boardtype; value: real;
begin
  if B is a leaf then return(payoff(B))
  else begin
    if mode = MAX then value := -INF else value := INF;
    for each child C of board B do
      if mode = MAX then value := max(value, search(C, MIN))
      else value := min(value, search(C, MAX));
    return(value)
  end
end;

